# TEST_PANIC_ONCE(NAME) expands to test_panic_NAME() whose body is expected to
# terminate the process with PANIC, i.e., with exit(-1), which leaks everything
# the body allocated. Suppressing all of it is deliberate: it is what makes
# make check-valgrind report no memory leaks for this kind of test. Keep the
# wildcard as it is -- the whole test_panic_* subtree must be covered.
# Do not anchor this on the runPanicTest() frame instead: that function is
# static with a single call site and gets inlined away.
{
   test_panic
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: all
   ...
   fun:test_panic_*
   ...
}
{
   openLogFile
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: all
   ...
   fun:openLogFile
   fun:main
}
